 "scenes": [
  {
   "id": "intro",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Instruction pipelines overlap instructions. Arithmetic pipelines overlap the steps inside one operation, like a floating point add."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "head"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Arithmetic pipelines"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Here are the seven stages."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "stages"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The number format, then the adder: its four stages, subtraction and its edge cases, and its timing."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[0..=3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Then multiply and divide, how many stages each takes, and why division is the odd one out."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[4..=6]"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "format",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 1: a floating point number has a sign, a mantissa and an exponent."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 1 of 7: the format"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "stages"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "fmt"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "By hand, we work in decimal: a mantissa times 10 to an exponent."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "fmt[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The hardware does the same in binary. In IEEE single precision the stored exponent has a bias of 127, which matters for multiply and divide."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "fmt[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "fmt[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Normalized means the first mantissa digit is not zero. In our decimal form, 0.9504, not 0.0950."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "fmt[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "fmt[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Why pipeline this? Each operation is a chain of dependent steps, and scientific loops repeat the same operation thousands of times."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "fmt"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "why"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[0..=1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "So with one stage per step, a new operation enters every cycle, and one result leaves every cycle."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[2]"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "add",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 2: the floating point adder has four stages. Add X equals 0.9504 times 10 cubed, and Y equals 0.8200 times 10 squared."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 2 of 7: the adder"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "why"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "add"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "addx"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 1, compare exponents: subtract them. 3 minus 2 is 1, so Y's exponent is smaller by 1."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "add.s1"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "addx[0][1]",
       "value": "3 − 2 = 1",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 2, align: shift the smaller number's mantissa right by that difference. Y becomes 0.0820 times 10 cubed. Now both have the same exponent."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "add.s2"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "addx[1][1]",
       "value": "Y = 0.0820 × 10³",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 3, add the mantissas: 0.9504 plus 0.0820 is 1.0324, times 10 cubed."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "add.s3"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "addx[2][1]",
       "value": "0.9504 + 0.0820 = 1.0324 × 10³",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 4, normalize: 1.0324 has overflowed past the point. Shift it right once and add 1 to the exponent: 0.10324 times 10 to the 4."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "add.s4"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "addx[3][1]",
       "value": "0.10324 × 10⁴",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Edge case: always shift the smaller number, right. Shifting the larger one left would lose its leading digits."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "compare → align (shift smaller right) → add → normalize"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "sub",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 3: subtraction uses the same four stages. To compute X minus Y, flip Y's sign, and add."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 3 of 7: subtract and normalize"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "add"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "addx"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "sub"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sub[3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The same X and Y: after aligning, 0.9504 minus 0.0820 is 0.8684 times 10 cubed. It is already normalized, so stage 4 does nothing."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sub[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The sum we just did overflowed instead, so stage 4 shifted right by one."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sub[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The hard case: subtracting nearly equal numbers. 0.5000 minus 0.4990 is 0.0010. Two leading zeros."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sub[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 4 must shift left by two and subtract 2 from the exponent: 0.1000 times 10 to the 0. So the normalizer must shift both ways, and count leading zeros for the left shift."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "sub[2][2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Edge case: whether the mantissas are really added or subtracted depends on the signs as well as the operation. Adding a negative number is a subtraction."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "normalize: overflow → shift right · leading zeros → shift left"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "timing",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 4: time the adder. Its stages take 60, 70, 100 and 80 nanoseconds, and each latch takes 10."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 4 of 7: timing the adder"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "sub"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "tm"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "As in video 8: the clock is the slowest stage plus the latch, 100 plus 10, which is 110 nanoseconds. Without the pipeline, one add takes the sum: 310."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "tm[0][3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "tm",
       "delay": 0.6
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "tmm",
       "delay": 0.6
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "So the speedup can approach 310 over 110, about 2.82, not 4, because the add stage is the slow one."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "tmm[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "tmm[1]"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "mul",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 5: multiplication is simpler in one way: no aligning. Exponents add and mantissas multiply."
