    {
     "say": {
      "en": "4.0 is too big, so normalize by shifting right: 0.40 times 10 to the 4."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "div.d3"
      },
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "divx[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "divx[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "With the bias, subtracting removes it, so add 127 back once: 133 minus 129 plus 127 is 131. And dividing by zero must give infinity or raise an exception."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "divx[4]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "divx[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "divx[4]",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Now the important part: the mantissa division is iterative. It produces the quotient a few bits at a time, reusing the same hardware."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "div"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "divx"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "dalg"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dalg[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Restoring and non-restoring division subtract and shift, one bit per step. SRT uses a table to pick two or more bits per step, but it is still a loop."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dalg[0..=1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Newton–Raphson and Goldschmidt find one over the divisor by repeated multiplication, which doubles the correct bits each time. But they occupy the multiplier."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "dalg[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Either way, the same hardware is busy until the quotient is done. So a new divide cannot start every cycle: division is not fully pipelined."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "divide: iterative · a new divide waits for the last one"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
